  "direct_findings": [
    "The historical #384–#387 failures coincide with 3.0-second wall receipt-age limits being exceeded by low-rate estimator_flags/land_detected while their simulation source ages remain below the retained 1.5-second source-age limit.",
    "#389 reached the ready map/VIO preconditions and passed the five-second combined gate with the 4.0-second run-local overlay; 39 fresh bridge detail samples fell in the gate window. In the same recorded telemetry, the longest sampled interval meeting all canonical 3.0-second receipt limits was 2.843 seconds, shorter than the required five seconds.",
    "#390 passed the same five-second gate. PX4 pre_flight_checks_pass became true and the bridge advanced through REQUEST_ARM to TAKEOFF after the accepted EnableOffboard request. During TAKEOFF, clock mapping reported clock_mapping_rate_out_of_bounds; mapped odometry wall age reached 0.434 seconds against its unchanged 0.3-second limit, so the bridge entered LANDING. The vehicle ended LANDED and disarmed. No navigation action goal was sent, and the harness did not observe ACTIVE.",
    "#388 showed all PX4 telemetry fresh under the overlay, but the VINS adapter locked on propagated_from_future and map occupied point count stayed zero, so it did not test the combined startup gate."
  ],
